{"name":"Mischief Mouse","hex":"#b7bab9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mischief","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Conduct that playfully causes petty annoyance.","A playfully annoying action."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To do a mischief to; to harm.","To slander."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mischief"},{"term":"mouse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any mammal of the many rodent families (especially Muridae) that have a small body and a long tail.","Such a rodent that is of the genus Mus."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move cautiously or furtively, in the manner of a mouse (the rodent) (frequently used in the phrasal verb to mouse around).","To hunt or catch mice (the rodents), usually of cats. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mischief","blocks":[{"text":"The more common use of mischief is an “action or conduct that annoys or vexes; esp., such as may cause trivial evil, annoyance, or trouble to others” - Webster’s International Dictionary."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Brueckner-Schile-Mischief.jpeg/330px-Brueckner-Schile-Mischief.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mischief","wikidata":"Q332970"},{"title":"Mouse","blocks":[{"text":"A mouse is a small rodent, characteristically known to have a pointed snout, small rounded ears, a body-length scaly tail, and a high breeding rate. The best known mouse species is the common house mouse. Mice are widely available as pets, but not as popular as some other rodents. In some places, certain kinds of field mice are locally common. They are known to invade homes for food and shelter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/%D0%9C%D1%8B%D1%88%D1%8C_2.jpg/330px-%D0%9C%D1%8B%D1%88%D1%8C_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wik